Z||000045||Blacktree||12-19-2001||02:49 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Spoken like a true dumb ass.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> Just because you don't like it doesn't make it junk.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>WHOA!!! Easy there, killer! Don't take things so personally. One man's junk is another man's treasure, we all know that. Just like some people consider rap/urban music to be junk, others consider rock/metal to be junk. To each his/her own.<P>I happen to like rock, metal, grunge, alterna-metal, some techno, and classical (yes, classical) music. If someone were to say that some music I like was junk, I'd just shrug my shoulders and say "OK, whatever".<P>Getting back on topic... here are some tunes I like to listen to whilst driving around town:<P><B>The distance</B> --Cake<BR><B>Enter the fold</B> --Filter<BR><B>Hey man, nice shot</B> --Filter<BR><B>Bled for days</B> --StaticX<BR><B>When worlds collide</B> --Powerman5000<BR><B>Blue Monday (remake)</B> --Orgy<BR><B>Click click boom</B> --Saliva<BR><B>Isolated</B> --Scrape<BR><B>Halo</B> --Soil<BR><B>Shock the monkey (remake)</B> --Coal Chamber (with Ozzy)<BR><B>Dig</B> --Mudvein<BR><B>Last resort</B> --Papa Roach<BR><B>The Blue Danube</B> --Johann Strauss<P>...and that's just a start   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Blacktree (edited 12-19-2001).]||||reg||1
